 are irrevocable and feasible after every prefix. The arrival order may depend measurably on all samples, values, and the seed, and only the offline optimum must be integrable.\n\nA supporting hidden-vector selection result for fixed nonnegative matroid weights gives expected worst-order reward at least $2^{-293}$ times the optimum, again with a finite seed law and prefix feasibility.","title":"One-sample matroid prophet inequalities against an almighty adversary","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/111.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":null,"reading":"reading:6f7006ce46b1efe4ff8f72da","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":"None; the hidden-vector selection result (constant 2^{-293}) is an extra supporting statement.","reading":"reading:4f3a0f3a50124d58c99ea7ad","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:6f7006ce46b1efe4ff8f72da","reading:4f3a0f3a50124d58c99ea7ad"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's 