dates. Prefer a producer main-result Lean object with an available target.","paired_statement":"r:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026:thm:main","paired_statements":["r:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026:thm:main"],"pairing_state":"candidate-pairing","scope_context":"family-readings"},"source_associations":[],"statements":[{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:b30dcc243db952f670fc7d87fba42c91edd8c79ec66c4dfd4e722e5b80239411","grain":"paper-statement","id":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026#thm:main"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/33bd30240cfb8ee3d41d3960.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Theorem","id":"r:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026:thm:main","manuscript_id":"p:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","name":"thm:main","printed_number":"1.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/introduction.tex","label":"thm:main","line":24,"manuscript":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","statement_sha256":"5b15fcbe35d7d2d9ba1b834cce7fa7a864793c5c4a62c4b98e38d91cd914b479"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026.html#thm:main","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","file":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":24,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5b15fcbe35d7d2d9ba1b834cce7fa7a864793c5c4a62c4b98e38d91cd914b479","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:202193e6deddb8284717c0a6f1800d0732acea9bd7757bf793dd792ce014c143","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L24"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a measurable online selection rule, independent of the value\ndistributions, with the following property. Let $M=(E,\\mathcal I)$ be any\nfinite known labeled matroid, and let $(S_e,V_e:e\\in E)$ be mutually\nindependent nonnegative real random variables, with $S_e$ and $V_e$ having\nthe same arbitrary law $D_e$. Assume\n$\\Ex[\\OPT_M(V)]<\\infty$. The rule receives exactly the sample vector $S$\nbefore arrivals and uses a seed $R$ independent of $S,V$.\n\nFor every measurable permutation rule $\\pi$ depending on $M$, the laws\n$(D_e)$, $S$, $V$, and $R$, the rule accepts an independent set $A$,\nirrevocably deciding at each arrival using only the available history, and\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main}\n \\Ex\\left[\\sum_{e\\in A}V_e\\right]\n       \\ge 2^{-310}\\Ex[\\OPT_M(V)].\n\\end{equation}"},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:cc2e908d446ff02224d32461833d4318fb84a03f82e6412aadb3060920300301","grain":"paper-statement","id":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026#prop:hidden"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/e9acec999a7394629a0b2096.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Proposition","id":"r:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026:prop:hidden","manuscript_id":"p:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","name":"prop:hidden","printed_number":"2.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/setup.tex","label":"prop:hidden","line":23,"manuscript":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","statement_sha256":"5a56f8533eb3587aeba02fb3a5c2cfb58b826d37a44925d8cd3fb95d8e823b97"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026.html#prop:hidden","section":2,"section_title":"A fixed-vector formulation","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","file":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/setup.tex","line":23,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5a56f8533eb3587aeba02fb3a5c2cfb58b826d37a44925d8cd3fb95d8e823b97","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/setup.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:47f74ccbb7b99d8afeb8de937021a6b41ae786fe290812496062b752c3f8332f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/setup.tex#L23"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:hidden}\nThere is a measurable rule in the fixed-vector formulation that is feasible for every\nrealization and every permutation, and for every $w\\in[0,\\infty)^E$ satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:hidden-guarantee}\n \\Ex_R\\left[\\min_{\\pi}\\sum_{e\\in A(w,R,\\pi)}w_e\\right]\n \\ge 2^{-293}\\OPT_M(w).\n\\end{equation}\nIts revealed mask is selected before any weights are seen."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:3015171c286bb5e82588fd9dce20b40789e2cf17b44723b9e8523da3e62bd49e","grain":"paper-statement","id":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026#cor:secretary"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/7f59af23bb093e650df161ee.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Corollary","id":"r:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026:cor:secretary","manuscript_id":"p:One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","name":"Order-oblivious selection with full-seed visibility","printed_number":"7.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","binding":{"file":"build/sections/secretary.tex","label":"cor:secretary","line":21,"manuscript":"One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026","statement_sha256":"79877c278a0b59a8e1b6fdd13d0f2fd0de9f32d9b77b7f9dcae0c6fd8a953836"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"recorded","reading_page":"papers/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026.html#cor:secretary","section":7,"section_title":"An order-oblivious secretary consequence","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","file":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/secretary.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"79877c278a0b59a8e1b6fdd13d0f2fd0de9f32d9b77b7f9dcae0c6fd8a953836","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/secretary.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:d1c0f2268699cd36e06cfe95e2b229ce218259e8647f31a940f222e305b1679d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/One-Sample-Suffices-for-Matroid-Prophet-Inequalities-against-an-Almighty-Adversary-September-23-2026/build/sections/secretary.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:secretary}\nFor each known finite labeled matroid $M=(E,\\mathcal I)$, there is one\nmeasurable randomized online rule $\\mathcal S_M$ with the following\nproperty. Fix any vector $w\\in[0,\\infty)^E$ of finite nonnegative weights\nbefore all rule and arrival randomness. Without knowing $w$, the rule\ndraws its complete initial seed $Q$, independently of a uniformly random\npermutation $\\sigma$ of $E$, and fixes a possibly random prefix length\n$K$ before any arrival. It observes the first $K$ label--weight pairs of\n$\\sigma$ in order and rejects those labels.\n\nAfter this ordered prefix is observed and before any suffix arrival, an\nadversary may know $M$, the entire fixed vector $w$, the ordered prefix,\nand the complete seed $Q$, including $K$, the branch choice, and unused\ncoins. It may choose any\nmeasurable permutation $\\tau$ of the remaining labels as a function of\nthis information. The rule is not told the future suffix order and decides\nirrevocably at each suffix arrival while maintaining an independent set.\nWriting $A_{\\mathcal S}$ for its accepted set, for every such adversary,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:secretary-guarantee}\n \\Ex\\left[\\sum_{e\\in A_{\\mathcal S}}w_e\\right]\n \\ge 2^{-293}\\OPT_M(w).\n\\end{equation}\nThe expectation is over the rule seed and random prefix, and over any\nadversary randomization. The adversary cannot alter the random-prefix law\nor choose the weights after observing the seed or prefix."}],"unavailable_check_reports":[]}
